      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-184025",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to construct a direct proof of the following statement:\n\n> $m$ and $n$ are even integers only if $mn - 2$ is even.\n\nA proof schema is outlined below. Fill in the missing entries.\n\nLet $m$ and $n$ be {{field-1}} integers. Then,\n$2a + 1$ {{field-2}} {{field-3}}\nfor some {{field-4}}.\n\nBy substituting the above into {{field-5}}, we can show that\n$2c$ {{field-6}}\nwhere $c$ is {{field-7}}.\n\nTherefore, since $mn - 2$ {{field-8}} a multiple of $2$, we conclude that $mn - 2$ is {{field-9}}."
